    <p>This English version and guide are made by <strong>CoffeeBns</strong>: <a href="https://twitch.tv/coffeebns" target="_blank" rel="noopener">twitch.tv/coffeebns</a> and <a href="https://youtube.com/@CoffeeBns" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youtube.com/@CoffeeBns</a>.</p>
    <p><strong>How these numbers were made.</strong> Every run used the simulator's own rules engine. A rules-based strategy played them, making each choice from what a player can see. There's no AI involved: it's a set of scoring rules whose weights were tuned for these rules by trying each value and keeping whichever vaulted more Rainbows. This data set took <span data-g="totalRuns"></span> runs and <span data-g="minutes"></span> minutes. The rules follow the season's video reveal and what players have since seen live. The rarity odds come from players' shared boards: an inmate behind a door is 40% Normal, 38% Magic, 12% Rare, 8% Legendary and 2% Supreme, and a Replace brings in 42%, 34%, 11.5%, 9.5% and 2.5%, always of another beast. From the same boards: a run starts with 4 inmates out (3 in about 1 run in 20), 72% of runs start with a special event, each event the warden sets off is followed by a new one 88% of the time, and the warden's office comes up among the doors about 1 morning in 4 when it's in reach. Other odds and limits are practice values and may differ from the live game: each day has one consume or one Replace, not both, over a 20-day drill. The full tables are in the <a href="https://github.com/blahdot3h/tartarus-simulator/tree/main/tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener">strategy lab's notes</a>.</p>
